# Keep GitHub in Sync with Deployments

This repo previously drifted ~5 weeks behind production because changes
were deployed straight to Databricks (`deploy.sh` / `sync_scpo.sh` +
`deploy_scpo.sh` / `databricks bundle deploy`) without ever being committed
or pushed to GitHub (`spensten-byte/Cursor-Rally-Work-Tracker`).

## Rule

Whenever you make a **real code change** (not just local experimentation)
and deploy it to either app (PaSE and/or SCPO), commit it and push to
`origin/main` in the same working session — don't leave it deployed-but-
uncommitted.

- Commit with a clear message describing what changed and why.
- Push after confirming the deploy succeeded (don't push broken code, but
  don't let working deploys sit uncommitted either).
- If a change is still experimental / not yet deployed, it's fine to hold
  off on committing until it's confirmed working in production.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, `.databrickscfg`, or anything already
  excluded by `.gitignore`.

If you're unsure whether something counts as a "real update" worth
committing (e.g. a one-off debug script or a reverted experiment), ask the
user before committing.
